title Caravan avow -- the plan says on the record what it makes of the finding against it
prompt Autonomous loop -- pick up the running thread, take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first, close open agent-closable reds first, send each finished increment.
think Loaded KYRI.md and RADIANT_STYLE.md first, so the voice shaped the lap from the first token, then the living card, then the top three rows of the log index and the newest log's recommend line.
think Standfast first: walked crux/REDS.md for open agent-closable reds. %97 closed on metal `20260820.030440`; %73 is booked to the chunking-storage horizon by design rather than open. Nothing to halt the line, so constructive work was clear to begin.
think The running thread came off the newest log's recommend line rather than off the card. The deem rung had just landed, and its recommend named the next crux exactly: the arc gives an operator a third hand's word and gives the plan no obligation whatever toward it, so a supervisor may publish a finding against itself beside `carried out whole` every run forever and never once let it touch what it does next.
think Named the rung under the Comlink tendency -- clear, fun, safe. Grepped the module for collisions: `heed`, `abide`, `answer`, `reply`, `amend`, and `own` are all already spoken for in the arc; `avow` is free, warm, and says exactly what it does. Its two words needed care too -- `Plea` already owns `.accepts`, so the plan's own word became `.concedes` beside `.dissents`.
think Read the whole deem tier before writing a line of it -- the Report nesting, the accessor chain, the note io, the harness that seats the wire, the fold-check chain, and the two measured runs -- then diffed refer.rye against deem.rye to learn the exact mechanical shape a new tier takes: the previous alias renamed through, one accessor added at the wrapped tier, every deeper accessor gaining one `.inner`.
think Shaped the rung around one honest asymmetry. Every note this arc has reached outward for -- the reader's reply, the third hand's finding -- is written by a hand the plan does not own, precisely so a supervisor can never grade the objection against it. An avowal is the opposite kind of record on purpose: the plan answering for itself, in its own hand. That is not the supervisor judging its own case; it is the supervisor being made to speak, which is the only thing the silence was costing.
think Held the line that answering is not yielding. The rung asks for a word and never for agreement -- a plan may concede the finding or keep its own word and say so where the finding is read, and both are proven on the wire as separate runs. A rung that forced agreement would have let a third hand decide the work, which the deem rung's own law forbids.
think Made the avowal echo the finding byte for byte. A plan that answered this argument before may still hold its word on an older verdict, and publishing that beside today's finding would tell an operator the plan spoke to something it never spoke to -- so `AvowMismatched` is the rung itself, refused by name.
obs The UNHEARD probe found a real ordering flaw rather than confirming a guess. The first cut read the published finding with `orelse return error.AvowUnfound` before consulting the refusal ladder, so a run that heard nothing refused `AvowUnfound` where the ladder promised `AvowUnheard`. Fixed at the root: the read now supplies the ladder rather than short-circuiting it, and every refusal is reached by argument in the order the doc names. Measurement beat memory -- the probe was the only thing that could have caught it.
obs Both measured runs now read the finding, unlike the deem lap where one plan read and one did not. That is what makes the parting honest: every number beneath this rung stands still under both marks, and only the answering to the finding moves.
obs A judge check inherited from the deem lap expected the bare run to read zero findings, which stopped being true the moment both marks read one. Retired it and replaced it with the pair that is now true -- both marks leave zero cases waiting and zero unanswered -- rather than loosening the check.
obs The witness records the probe that taught the rung its shape, so a future reader learns the ordering law from the file that proves it rather than from this log alone.
loom witness=caravan_avow_witness rungs=76 sing=GREEN refusals=5 red_paths=6 avow_bytes=2
file caravan/avow.rye the rung -- Avow, the two-byte avowal echoing its finding, five refusals, the measurement, the note io, and the avowing as the last act of the run
file tools/caravan_avow_witness.rish the witness -- five refusals by name, six RED paths named on metal, the planted control, and every number beneath the rung asserted still
file tools/caravan_suite_witness.rish avow registered in the choir; roster guard proves the bijection at 76
file caravan/README.md the avow section, in the arc's own voice, beside the deem rung it answers
file crux/REMEMBER.md live edge refreshed to the avowing; the deem edge condensed into the prior-edges line, cairn 42f333eb6c
recommend keep-going the arc now corrects a record, carries the correction, hears the answer, records the disagreement, escorts the word, bounds the objection, stands its standing, tells the raiser, reads their reply, carries a live quarrel past the run that heard it, makes the inheriting run answer for it, lets its holder close it, says how long a standing one has stood, reads that age aloud, puts a long-standing one before a hand that is neither party, reads back what that hand made of it, and now makes the plan answer that finding on the record -- so the question above is what a plan's own word obliges it to do: a supervisor may publish `the plan takes the finding, and says the work is owed another look` beside `carried out whole` every run forever, and nothing anywhere makes a conceded finding change one thing the next run does.
